1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:01,925
The agent says it finished.

2
00:00:01,925 --> 00:00:04,240
You still need to know what it actually did.

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,508
Did it stay within the job you approved?

4
00:00:06,898 --> 00:00:08,734
Run logs help engineers.

5
00:00:08,734 --> 00:00:12,201
For everyone else, they are dense and easy to misread.

6
00:00:12,201 --> 00:00:14,206
A green check says the run ended.

7
00:00:14,206 --> 00:00:16,612
It does not say the run was authorized.

8
00:00:17,062 --> 00:00:21,768
Agent Receipt turns the JSON record you provide into a review backed by evidence.

9
00:00:21,768 --> 00:00:25,750
It reviews the run afterward, using only the record in front of you.

10
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:30,112
Start with a record-oriented JSON file from an agent or workflow.

11
00:00:30,112 --> 00:00:34,668
Before parsing anything, Agent Receipt hashes the file's exact bytes.

12
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:39,200
If the fields are unfamiliar, you confirm the paths and what each value means.

13
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,619
All ten selected records are counted.

14
00:00:41,619 --> 00:00:43,628
Unknown values stay unknown.

15
00:00:44,038 --> 00:00:46,605
The run log does not decide what was allowed.

16
00:00:46,605 --> 00:00:48,327
You enter that separately.

17
00:00:48,327 --> 00:00:53,575
Name the systems, actions, egress rules, and approvals that were in force for this run.

18
00:00:53,965 --> 00:00:56,623
Here, the trace stays within that envelope.

19
00:00:56,623 --> 00:00:59,458
The finding applies to this file and these rules.

20
00:00:59,458 --> 00:01:05,732
The receipt keeps the file digest, mapping manifest, record accounting, and policy decisions together.

21
00:01:06,222 --> 00:01:07,870
Now look at a different run.

22
00:01:07,870 --> 00:01:10,830
A spreadsheet action ends with an unknown outcome.

23
00:01:10,830 --> 00:01:14,285
The same run sends a customer email without approval.

24
00:01:14,285 --> 00:01:18,212
The policy engine flags both deviations in the supplied trace.

25
00:01:18,212 --> 00:01:22,858
Open a finding to see the rule, normalized event, and retained source record.

26
00:01:23,268 --> 00:01:26,838
If the trace is incomplete, the answer stays incomplete.

27
00:01:26,838 --> 00:01:32,545
This OTLP run has one material span Agent Receipt cannot parse, and no final status.

28
00:01:32,545 --> 00:01:34,279
Every span is counted.

29
00:01:34,279 --> 00:01:37,239
Missing evidence cannot become a clean verdict.

30
00:01:37,749 --> 00:01:43,092
Export the brief, receipt, and proposal-only recovery plan as one evidence packet.

31
00:01:43,092 --> 00:01:46,194
The browser verifier replays eight checks offline.

32
00:01:46,194 --> 00:01:48,810
Change one claim, and the packet fails.

33
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:54,518
Granite sees only minimized, redacted facts and citation IDs it is allowed to use.

34
00:01:54,518 --> 00:01:56,558
Code still decides the verdict.

35
00:01:56,558 --> 00:01:59,612
The deterministic fallback works without Granite.

36
00:02:00,152 --> 00:02:02,987
IBM Bob built the first trust-critical layer.

37
00:02:02,987 --> 00:02:04,996
Later work is logged separately.

38
00:02:05,586 --> 00:02:07,428
When an agent says it's done...

39
00:02:07,428 --> 00:02:08,559
Check the work.
